      "v": 2,
      "zh": "「人子啊，葡萄树比别样树有甚么强处？葡萄枝比众树枝有甚么好处？",
      "en": "“Son of man, of all the woody branches among the trees of the forest, what happens to the wood of the vine?[NOTE:1]",
      "notes": [
        "Most modern translations take the statement as a comparison (“how is vine wood better than any forest wood?”) based on the preposition מִן (min). But a comparison should have a word as an adjective or stative verb designating a quality, i.e., a word for “good/better” is lacking. The preposition is translated above in its partitive sense.sn Comparing Israel to the wood of the vine may focus on Israel’s inferiority to the other nations. For the vine imagery in relation to Israel and the people of God, see Ps 80:8-13; John 15:1-7; Rom 11:17-22."
